<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Puig</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1237</span> · Also known as Battle of El Puig · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Puig was fought in 1237 at El Puig, a hill north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>, where Aragonese troops holding a fortress built on the orders of James I defeated an army sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zayyan-ibn-mardanish">Zayyan ibn Mardanish</a>, ruler of Valencia. The victory secured the Christian foothold near the city and prepared James I's siege of Valencia, which surrendered in 1238.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-puig.jpg" alt="Battle of the Puig" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andreu Marçal de Sax / Andrès Marçal de Sas · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batalla_del_Puig_por_Marzal_de_Sas_(1410-20).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
